tags: int-ops, int_ops_per_sec

A score of one core: integer operations per second.

The value is an integer, in operation per second. Example: 2500000. More is better. The
node measures it with one process, so it is what one core does, in a guest of the
architecture of the announcement. The method is fixed: the static program BusyBox 1.37.0
that the formal names as a document for the instruction set of the guest, and the loop
that the formal gives. A faster method (for example a compiled program) is another
benchmark.

The statistic is one run of at least 2 seconds. It is not a mean of runs and not a
percentile. A score that must be stable is another benchmark.

In an announcement, an absent score is not measured, never 0. In a requirement
(Resources.benchmarks), the node compares its score with "greater than or equal" at
each placement. A node that did not measure the score refuses.

=== formal
class=benchmark
clock=the first number of the file /proc/uptime of the guest (the page proc_uptime(5) of the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:0547755fe776075c828d11f43fd868af1338cc669c8f0b4ac8a72dddcea42698), in hundredths of a second
method=a loop of the ash of the tool: x=(x*1103515245+12345)&2147483647, starting at x=1; read the clock after each 1000 steps; stop at the first read at or after 200 hundredths of a second
name=int-ops
place=the benchmarks of a container or of an architecture
process=one process (definition 3.279 (Process) of the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:5dd925be58ed836308859cb1796d9006a7ff6b32eaa1281fd0f28c4604773ed9): the score is what one core (the concept 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:74b75cc69cfa93ec7b96b07316fee2be3fe54afb24972ecd74002523e374c29a) does
score=floor(steps*100/elapsed hundredths of a second)
stat=one run on an idle guest: the rate over one window of at least 2 seconds; no mean of runs and no percentile
tools=the static program BusyBox 1.37.0, with its applets awk, ash, dd and sha256sum, for the instruction set of the architecture: the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:d4206562a06c19d044c16876f9da490211093cfa1816959ea4ec2c77459e33c1 for the concept 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:bacad9da2c43fb7a1edf0a3bd79143d019a754e3992591d3353fc058b9a03ab7, the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:6e44a4c142a0a543cd5e75dc52649178c83a4048542d32c73cb9b240d81733d2 for the concept 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:cc71d5ea3cf371762ecd300d4fd07d81f1b02c4759237179520f686579366784; the source of both is the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:acc624a0fc8771fb3195112fff9dcb741781d414ac3fcf823aaa244757198abc; it runs in a guest (the concept 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:b3469e385a533a222a75a1aeafb1a94b2795a9f689e302f034283e1d8cdceb38) of the architecture; for another instruction set the benchmark is not defined
unit=operation/second
